<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet xml:id="ws_5_5" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
<title>5.5 Practice Worksheet</title>


<exercise>
<introduction>
<p>
For each problem, suppose <m>t</m> is measured in years. Give the initial value, the continuous growth rate, the annual growth factor, and the annual growth rate.
</p>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>y=1450e^{0.72t}</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The initial value is <m>A = 1450</m> and the continuous growth rate is <m>k=0.72 = 72\%</m>. Then, <m>b=e^k = e^{0.72} = 2.05443</m> is the annual growth factor. The annual growth rate is <m>r=b-1 = 2.05443-1 = 1.05443 = 105.443\%</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>P(t)=10000e^{-0.48t}</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The initial value is <m>A = 10000</m> and the continuous growth rate is <m>k=-0.48=-48\%</m>. Then, <m>b=e^k = e^{-0.48} = 0.61878</m> is the annual growth factor. The annual growth rate is <m>r=b-1 = 0.61878 -1 = -0.38122 = -38.122\%</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>Q=27e^{1.65t}</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The initial value is <m>27</m> and the continuous growth rate is <m>k=1.65 = 165\%</m>. Then, <m>b=e^{k} = e^{1.65} = 5.2069</m> is the annual growth factor. The annual growth rate is <m>r = b -1 = 5.2069 - 1 = 4.2069 = 420.69\%</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
<m>f(t)=200e^{-0.02t}</m>
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The initial value is <m>200</m> and the continuous growth rate is <m>k = -0.02 = -2\%</m>. Then, <m>b=e^k = e^{-0.02} = 0.9802</m> is the annual growth factor. The annual growth rate is <m>r=b-1 = 0.9802 -1 = -0.0198 = -1.98\%</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


</exercise>


<exercise>
<introduction>
<p>
A trash dumpster starts with <m>5</m> pounds of garbage. Write a formula which represents the amount of garbage in the dumpster after <m>t</m> days given the following rates.
</p>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
The amount of garbage increases by <m>3</m> pounds per day.
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
This describes a linear relationship <m>y=mt+b</m> where the slope is <m>m=3</m> and the intercept is <m>b=5</m> so <m>y=3t+5</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
The amount of garbage increases by <m>3\%</m> per day.
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
This is an exponential relationship. The initial value is <m>A=5</m> and the growth rate is <m>r=3\% = 0.03</m> so the growth factor is <m>b=1+r = 1.03</m>. Therefore <m>y=5(1.03)^t</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
The amount of garbage increases at a continuous rate of <m>3\%</m> per day.
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
This is an exponential relationship. The initial value is <m>A=5</m> and the continuous growth rate is <m>k=3\% = 0.03</m>. Therefore <m>y=5 e^{0.03t}</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


</exercise>




<exercise>
<introduction>
<p>
A container with <m>1</m> liter of liquid is placed in a warm, arid environment. The liquid evaporates at a continuous rate of <m>2.3\%</m> per day.
</p>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
Write a function which represents the amount of liquid (in milliliters) in the container after <m>t</m> days.
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The initial value is <m>1</m> liter so <m>A=1000</m> milliliters (be careful on the units!) and the continuous growth rate is <m>k=-2.3\% = -0.023</m>. Therefore <m>y=1000 e^{-0.023t}</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
What is the daily decay rate?
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Recall that <m>k=-0.023</m> so <m>b=e^{k} = e^{-0.023} = 0.97726</m>. Thus the growth rate is <m>r=b-1 = -0.02274 = -2.274\%</m>, and then the decay rate is <m>2.274\%</m>.
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
How much liquid remains after <m>5</m> days?
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Using part (a), evaluate the function at <m>t=5</m> to get <m>y=1000e^{-0.023(5)} = 891.366</m> milliliters.
</p>
</solution>
</task>


</exercise>


<exercise>
<introduction>
<p>
Write a formula for each of the following.
</p>
</introduction>

<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
The amount of a radioactive substance present after <m>t</m> hours if there are initially <m>500</m> mg and the half-life is <m>9</m> hours.
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Here we have <m>A=500</m> being the initial value and <m>T=9</m> hours being the half-life. Therefore
<md>
y = 500 \pbr{\frac{1}{2}} ^{t /9}
</md> <em>See section 5.4 for this formula</em>
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
The value of a car after <m>t</m> years if the initial price is <m>\$26,\!000</m> and the car depreciates at a rate of <m>11\%</m> per year.
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The initial value <m>A=26000</m> and the growth rate is <m>r=-11\% = -0.11</m> so <m>b=1+r = 1+(-0.11) = 0.89</m>. Therefore
<md>
y = 26000\cdot (0.89)^t.
</md>
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
The value of a car after <m>t</m> years if the initial price is <m>\$33,\!000</m> and the car depreciates at a rate of <m>\$3,\!700</m> per year.
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
Because the value of the car decreases by a constant amount per year, this is a linear function (namely, not exponential). Therefore
<md>
y = -3700t + 33000.
</md>
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task workspace="1in">
<statement>
<p>
The population of a city in year <m>t</m> (measured in years after 2005) if the population in 2005 is <m>125,\!000</m> and the city is growing at a continuous rate of <m>3.1\%</m> per year.
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The initial value is <m>125000</m> and the continuous growth rate is <m>k=3.1\%=0.031</m>. Therefore
<md>
y = 125000 e^{0.031t}.
</md>
</p>
</solution>
</task>



<task>
<statement>
<p>
The number of ants in a colony if the initial colony size is <m>6000</m> ants and the number of ants increases by <m>2.7\%</m> each day.
</p>
</statement>
<solution>
<p>
The initial value is <m>A = 6000</m> and the growth rate <m>r=2.7\%=0.027</m> so <m>b=1+r=1.027</m>. Therefore
<md>
y = 6000(1.027)^t.
</md>
</p>
</solution>
</task>



</exercise>


</worksheet>